{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to take every change to agreed requirement text, including a rewording for precision and the removal of a requirement, through the same review and agreement before committing it.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to put every change to agreed requirement text through the same review and agreement before committing it. The text names two cases: a rewording for precision and the removal of a requirement.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_reviews_every_change_to_agreed_text]` is the only test marked for this requirement. It checks the bundled skill text, and these assertions cover the obligation:\n- `assert_phrases` requires the sentence \"Every change to agreed text, including a rewording for precision or removing a requirement, goes through steps 3 to 5 before it is committed\". `assert_phrases` calls `assert_text` on the collapsed `bundled_skill`, so line wrapping does not matter. The sentence names both cases the requirement lists, a rewording and a removal. It also gives the direction \"before it is committed\".\n- `step_of(\"habeas-requirements\", \"Sort the new and changed requirements into groups\")` must equal 3. `step_of` reads the numbered steps from `workflow_steps`. This ties \"steps 3 to 5\" to the review step actually being step 3, so renumbering would fail the test.\n- `description(\"habeas-requirements\")` must contain \"before changing code, tests, or requirement text\". This puts requirement-text changes in the skill's trigger.\n- Two `workflow.contains` assertions check the other gating wording. The first is the \"If the change adds, alters, or removes no observable behavior\" branch. The second tells the user which existing requirement covers a bug fix. Both support that requirement changes are the thing being gated.\n\n**Mutations the test would catch.** Dropping the sentence, narrowing it to exclude rewording or removal, dropping \"before it is committed\", or moving the review step away from step 3 would each fail an assertion. The helpers' assertions run in the test, so they count. I read `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` through a search. The asserted sentence is in the Workflow section, so the expected results match the requirement.\n\n**Gaps.** None found. The test does not separately check what steps 4 and 5 contain. The requirement does not specify those steps, so that is not a gap here. There are no acknowledgments.",
  "references": "9854ef5544b06bd0e771922109f2946991072b56097f87b408baa38f84a68c16",
